From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmytro Kostyshyn <dima.kostishen@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 14:44:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Server players show their health to the others at full health
 too

LivingEntity.DATA_HEALTH_ID is defined as 1 and set to the max health, so
vanilla's pairing (getNonDefaultValues) sends a player's 20 to everyone who
sees it. The hub left out exactly 20, so a client never had the health of
another player at full health: anything reading it (Horizon's bots, picking
living targets) took the player for not alive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0183TW2kCwgZukLd4gu1ykmr
---
 crates/horizon-client/src/lan/hub.rs | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/crates/horizon-client/src/lan/hub.rs b/crates/horizon-client/src/lan/hub.rs
index f2021aaf3f..aae35c0236 100644
--- a/crates/horizon-client/src/lan/hub.rs
+++ b/crates/horizon-client/src/lan/hub.rs
@@ -3334,7 +3334,9 @@ impl Hub {
         if let Some(bed) = bed.filter(|_| sleeping) {
             meta.push((14, serializer::OPTIONAL_BLOCK_POS, Value::OptPos(Some(bed))));
         }
-        if (health - 1.0).abs() > f32::EPSILON && health != 20.0 {
+        // LivingEntity.DATA_HEALTH_ID: defined as 1, then set to the max health. The pairing sends the values that
+        // are not the defined ones (getNonDefaultValues), so a player at full health shows its 20 to the others.
+        if (health - 1.0).abs() > f32::EPSILON {
             meta.push((9, serializer::FLOAT, Value::Float(health)));
         }
         if skin != 0 {
